; SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
; Steal This Pedal factory bank — slot 2
; GHOST SPRING
; POT0 = decay
; POT1 = drip / pick-transient injection
; POT2 = dispersion / dwell
; Wet-only output.  This is a spring-flavored network, not a literal model.
; Spin Computer adaptation: reduce late feedback from 0.84 to 0.40.
; The early dwell path also feeds the tank; their combined gain must stay <1.

PRE         MEM 431
AP1         MEM 37
AP2         MEM 61
AP3         MEM 109
AP4         MEM 181
TANK        MEM 11700
INPUT       EQU REG0
LPSTATE     EQU REG1
DRIP        EQU REG2
DIFFUSED    EQU REG3
TAIL        EQU REG4

; Average the inputs and form a crude transient/high-pass signal.
RDAX ADCL, 0.5
RDAX ADCR, 0.5
WRAX INPUT, 1.0
RDFX LPSTATE, 0.055
WRAX LPSTATE, 0.0
LDAX INPUT
RDAX LPSTATE, -1.0
MULX POT1
SOF 1.65, 0.0
WRAX DRIP, 0.0

; A short predelay makes the initial clank separate from the wash.
LDAX INPUT
SOF 0.62, 0.0
RDAX DRIP, 0.85
WRA PRE, 0.0
CLR
RDA PRE#, 1.0

; Short stretched allpasses create the spring-like dispersive chirp.
RDA AP1#, 0.63
WRAP AP1, -0.63
RDA AP2#, -0.57
WRAP AP2, 0.57
RDA AP3#, 0.51
WRAP AP3, -0.51
RDA AP4#, -0.46
WRAP AP4, 0.46
WRAX DIFFUSED, 0.0

; Dwell adds an earlier dispersed reflection back into the tank input.
LDAX POT2
SOF 0.50, 0.15
WRAX REG5, 0.0
CLR
RDA TANK+1873, 1.0
MULX REG5
RDAX DIFFUSED, 0.78
WRAX DIFFUSED, 0.0

; Dark, pot-controlled recirculation.
CLR
RDA TANK#, 1.0
RDFX TAIL, 0.12
WRAX TAIL, 1.0
MULX POT0
SOF 0.40, 0.0
RDAX DIFFUSED, 1.0
WRA TANK, 0.0

; Unequal taps make a wide, clangy stereo spring field.
CLR
RDA TANK+1541, 0.72
RDA TANK+4327, -0.38
RDA TANK+7883, 0.47
RDA TANK+10391, -0.24
WRAX DACL, 0.0
CLR
RDA TANK+2213, 0.66
RDA TANK+5891, 0.41
RDA TANK+9067, -0.36
RDA TANK+11279, 0.22
WRAX DACR, 0.0
